          %h2#References References
          %h3#general_2 General
          %p
            First indications for M-theory came from the observation that the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/double+dimensional+reduction"} double dimensional reduction
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/supermembrane"} supermembrane
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Green-Schwarz+sigma-model"} Green-Schwarz sigma-model
            on
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/11d+supergravity"} 11d supergravity
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/target+spacetimes"} target spacetimes
            (now called the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/M2-brane"} M2-brane
            yields the
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/type+IIA+superstring"} type IIA superstring
          %ul
            %li#DuffHoweInamiStelle87
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Michael+Duff"}> Michael Duff
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Paul+Howe"} Paul Howe
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kellogg+Stelle"} Kellogg Stelle
              = succeed "," do
                %em
                  Superstrings in
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi D
                        %mo =
                        %mn 10
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D=10
                  from Supermembranes in
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi D
                        %mo =
                        %mn 11
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D=11
              %strong 191
              (1987) 70 &amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1016/0370-2693(87)91323-2"}> doi:10.1016/0370-2693(87)91323-2
              \&amp;rbrack; and in:
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Michael+Duff"} Michael Duff
              (ed.)
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/The+World+in+Eleven+Dimensions"} The World in Eleven Dimensions
              205-206 (1987) &amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "http://inspirehep.net/record/245249"}> spire
              \&amp;rbrack;
          %p
            and the first statement of what came to be known as the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/duality+between+type+IIA+string+theory+and+M-theory"} duality between type IIA string theory and M-theory
            is due to:
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Paul+K.+Townsend"}> Paul K. Townsend
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em The eleven-dimensional supermembrane revisited
              %strong 350
              (1995) 184-187 &amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/9501068"}> arXiv:hep-th/9501068
              ,
              = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1016/0370-2693(95)00397-4"} doi:10.1016/0370-2693(95)00397-4
          %p A comprehensive collection of early articles is in
          %ul
            %li#Duff99
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Michael+Duff"}> Michael Duff
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/The+World+in+Eleven+Dimensions"}> The World in Eleven Dimensions
                  \: Supergravity, Supermembranes and M-theory
              = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                %a{:href => "https://www.crcpress.com/The-World-in-Eleven-Dimensions-Supergravity-supermembranes-and-M-theory/Duff/9780750306720"} ISBN:9780750306720
          %p
            For some time though the success of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/string+theory"} string theory
            in 10-dimensions caused resistence to the idea of a theory of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/membranes"} membranes
            in 11-dimensions, an account is in (
            %a{:href => "#Duff99"}> Duff 99
            ) and in brevity on the first pages of
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Michael+Duff"}> Michael Duff
              \:
              = succeed "," do
                %em M-history without the M
              %strong 57
              1 (2016) &amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1501.04098"}> arXiv:1501.04098
              ,
              = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1080/00107514.2014.992964"} doi:10.1080/00107514.2014.992964
          %p The article that convinced the community of M-theory was
          %ul
            %li#Witten95
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Edward+Witten"}> Edward Witten
              , esp. §2.2, §2.3 in:
              = succeed "," do
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/String+Theory+Dynamics+In+Various+Dimensions"} String Theory Dynamics In Various Dimensions
              %strong 443
              (1995) 85-126 &amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/9503124"}> arXiv:hep-th/9503124
              ,
              = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1016/0550-3213(95)00158-O"} doi:10.1016/0550-3213(95)00158-O
          %p
            A public talk announcing the conjecture that the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/non-perturbative+field+theory"} strong-coupling limit
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/type+IIA+string+theory"} type IIA string theory
            is
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/11-dimensional+supergravity"} 11-dimensional supergravity
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/KK-compactification"} KK-compactified
            on a circle is at 15:12 in
          %ul
            %li#Witten95Talk
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Edward+Witten"}> Edward Witten
              , talk at University of Southern California (1995) &amp;lbrack;video:
              %a{:href => "https://youtu.be/1HYa4wxqe8Y"}> YT
              \&amp;rbrack;
              %blockquote
                %p 19:33: “Ten years ago we had the embarrassment that there were five consistent string theories plus a close cousin, which was 11-dimensional supergravity.” (19:40): “I promise you that by the end of the talk we have just one big theory.”
          %p The term “M-theory” originates in
          %ul
            %li#HoravaWitten95
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Petr+Ho%C5%99ava"}> Petr Hořava
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Edward+Witten"} Edward Witten
              = succeed "," do
                %em Heterotic and Type I string dynamics from eleven dimensions
              %strong 460
              (1996) 506 &amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/9510209"}> arXiv:hep-th/9510209
              ,
              = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1016/0550-3213(95)00621-4"} doi:10.1016/0550-3213(95)00621-4
          %p as a “non-committed” shorthand for “membrane theory”
          %blockquote
            %p#NonCommittal
              As it has been proposed that the eleven-dimensional theory is a supermembrane theory but there are some reasons to doubt that interpretation, we will non-committally call it the M-theory, leaving to the future the relation of M to membranes. (
              %a{:href => "#HoravaWitten95"}> Hořava-Witten 95, p. 2
              )
          %p and
          %ul
            %li#Witten95
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Edward+Witten"}> Edward Witten
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Five-branes And M-Theory On An Orbifold
              %strong 463
              (1996) 383-397 &amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/9512219"}> arXiv:hep-th/9512219
              \&amp;rbrack;
          %p which coined the association
          %blockquote
            %p
              the eleven-dimensional “M-theory” (where M stands for magic, mystery, or membrane, according to taste) (
              %a{:href => "#Witten95"}> Witten 95, p. 1
              )
          %p that later gained much publicity:
          %ul
            %li#Witten98
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Edward+Witten"}> Edward Witten
              \:
              = succeed "," do
                %em Magic, Mystery, and Matrix
              %strong 45
              9 (1998) &amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "http://www.ams.org/notices/199809/witten.pdf"}> pdf
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/files/Witten-MagicMysteryMatrix.pdf", :title => "pdf"} pdf
              = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                %a{:href => "https://www.ams.org/notices/199810/199810FullIssue.pdf"} pdf
          %p
            The argument that the regularized
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/M2-brane"} M2-brane
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/worldvolume"} worldvolume
            theory is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/BFSS+matrix+model"} BFSS matrix model
            is discussed in
          %ul
            %li#NicolaiHelling98
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hermann+Nicolai"}> Hermann Nicolai
                , Robert Helling:
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Supermembranes and M(atrix) Theory
                %em
                  %a{:href => "https://inspirehep.net/conferences/971546"} ICTP Spring School on Nonperturbative Aspects of String Theory and Supersymmetric Gauge Theories
                (1998) 29-74 &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/9809103"}> arXiv:hep-th/9809103
                ,
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "https://inspirehep.net/literature/476366"} spire:476366
            %li#DasguptaNicolaiPlefka02
              %p
                Arundhati Dasgupta,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hermann+Nicolai"} Hermann Nicolai
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jan+Plefka"} Jan Plefka
                = succeed "," do
                  %em An Introduction to the Quantum Supermembrane
                %strong 8
                1 (2002) Rev. Mex. Fis.
                %strong 49S1
                (2003) 1-10 &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/0201182"}> arXiv:hep-th/0201182
                \&amp;rbrack;
          %p Recollections include the last paragraph of
          %ul
            %li#Witten14
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Edward+Witten"}> Edward Witten
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Adventures in Physics and Math
              %a{:href => "http://www.kyotoprize.org/en/laureates/commemorative_lectures/"} Kyoto Prize lecture
              2014 (
              %a{:href => "http://www.kyotoprize.org/wp/wp-content/uploads/2016/02/30kB_lct_EN.pdf"}> pdf
              ,
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/files/WittenKyotoPrizeLecture.pdf", :title => "pdf"} pdf
          %p The term became fully established with surveys including
          %ul
            %li#Duff96
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Michael+Duff"}> Michael Duff
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em M-Theory (the Theory Formerly Known as Strings)
                %strong 11
                (1996) 5623-5642 &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/9608117"}> arXiv:hep-th/9608117
                ,
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1142/S0217751X96002583"} doi:10.1142/S0217751X96002583
            %li#Duff98
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Michael+Duff"}> Michael Duff
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em The Theory Formerly Known as Strings
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "https://www.nikhef.nl/pub/services/biblio/bib_KR/sciam14395569.pdf"} pdf
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/files/DuffFormerlyStrings98.pdf", :title => "pdf"} pdf
            %li#Duff98b
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Michael+Duff"}> Michael Duff
                \:
                = succeed "," do
                  %em A Layman’s Guide to M-theory
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Trends in Mathematical Physics
                %strong 13
                (1999) 184-213 &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/9805177"}> arXiv:hep-th/9805177
                ,
                %a{:href => "https://cds.cern.ch/record/355721"} cds:355721
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1090/amsip/013"} doi:10.1090/amsip/013
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "https://www.ams.org/books/amsip/013"} ams:amsip/013
          %p
            Despite the magic and mystery, the relation to the original abbreviation for
            %em membrane-theory
            was highlighted again for instance in
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Paul+Townsend"}> Paul Townsend
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em
                  M(embrane) theory on
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mi T
                          %mn 0
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T^0
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/9708034"} arXiv:hep-th/9708034
          %p
            Early articles clarifying the relation to
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/type+II+string+theory"} type II string theory
            = succeed ":" do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/F-theory"} F-theory
          %ul
            %li#Schwarz95
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/John+Schwarz"}> John Schwarz
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em The Power of M Theory
                %strong 367
                (1996) 97-103 &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1016/0370-2693(95)01429-2"}> doi:10.1016/0370-2693(95)01429-2
                ,
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/9510086"} arXiv:hep-th/9510086
            %li#Johnson97
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Clifford+Johnson"}> Clifford Johnson
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em From M-theory to F-theory, with Branes
                %strong 507
                (1997) 227-244 &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1016/S0550-3213(97)00550-6"} doi:10.1016/S0550-3213(97)00550-6
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/9706155"} arXiv:hep-th/9706155
          %p
            The relation also to the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/heterotic+string"} heterotic string
            was understood in
            %a{:href => "#HoravaWitten95"} Hořava &amp; Witten 95
            see at
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Horava-Witten+theory"} Horava-Witten theory
          %p Early review and discussion:
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Paul+Townsend"}> Paul Townsend
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Four Lectures on M-theory
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Proceedings of the ICTP summer school on High Energy Physics and Cosmology
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/9612121"} arXiv:hep-th/9612121
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "https://inspirehep.net/literature/427195"} spire:427195
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hermann+Nicolai"}> Hermann Nicolai
                \:
                = succeed "," do
                  %em On M-Theory
                = succeed "," do
                  %strong 20
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/9801090"} arXiv:hep-th/9801090
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1007/BF02702349"} doi:10.1007/BF02702349
              %blockquote
                %p
                  (focus on
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/U-duality"} U-duality
                  and early idea of
                  = succeed ")" do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/exceptional+field+theory"} exceptional field theory
            %li#ObersPioline98
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Niels+A.+Obers"}> Niels A. Obers
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Boris+Pioline"} Boris Pioline
                = succeed "," do
                  %em U-duality and M-Theory
                %strong 318
                (1999) 113-225 &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/9809039"}> arXiv:hep-th/9809039
                ,
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1016/S0370-1573(99)00004-6"} doi:10.1016/S0370-1573(99)00004-6
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/John+Schwarz"}> John Schwarz
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Introduction to M Theory and AdS/CFT Duality
                %em Quantum Aspects of Gauge Theories, Supersymmetry and Unification
                Lecture Notes in Physics
                = succeed "," do
                  %strong 525
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/9812037"} arXiv:hep-th/9812037
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1007/BFb0104239"} doi:10.1007/BFb0104239
              %blockquote
                %p
                  (with an eye towards
                  = succeed ")" do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/AdS%2FCFT+duality"} AdS/CFT duality
          %p Further developments:
          %ul
            %li#Carlevaro06
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Luca+Carlevaro"}> Luca Carlevaro
              \:
              = succeed "," do
                %em Three approaches to M-theory
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "https://libra.unine.ch/handle/123456789/16186"} hdl:123456789/16186
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "https://libra.unine.ch/server/api/core/bitstreams/b5eedf5f-8029-4700-83cb-806d0737a669/content"} pdf
              = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                %a{:href => "https://inspirehep.net/literature/1253257"} spire:1253257
              %blockquote
                %p
                  (
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/BFSS+matrix+model"} BFSS matrix model
                  and
                  = succeed "-enhancement," do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/orthosymplectic+super+Lie+algebra"}
                      %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                        %semantics
                          %mrow
                            %mi 𝔬𝔰𝔭
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mn 1
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                            %mn 32
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathfrak{osp}(1\vert 32)
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/heterotic+M-theory"} heterotic M-theory
                  = succeed "-" do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/E10"}
                      %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                        %semantics
                          %mrow
                            %msub
                              %mi E
                              %mn 10
                          %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E_{10}
                  = succeed ")" do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/U-duality"} U-duality
          %p
            Surveys of the discussion of E-series
            = succeed "/" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kac-Moody+algebras"} Kac-Moody algebras
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kac-Moody+groups"} Kac-Moody groups
            in the context of M-theory include
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                Sophie de Buyl,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Kac-Moody Algebras in M-theory
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://theses.ulb.ac.be/ETD-db/collection/available/ULBetd-06072006-153117/unrestricted/kmalgebrasinmth.pdf"} pdf
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Paul+Cook"}> Paul Cook
                ,
                %em Connections between Kac-Moody algebras and M-theory
                PhD thesis (
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/0711.3498"}> arXiv:0711.3498
                )
          %p
            Review in the context of
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/duality+in+string+theory"} duality in string theory
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Sebastian+De+Haro"}> Sebastian De Haro
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jeremy+Butterfield"} Jeremy Butterfield
              %p
                %em> The Philosophy and Physics of Duality
                , Cambridge University Press (2025) &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2508.01616"}> arXiv:2508.01616
                ,
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "https://global.oup.com/academic/product/the-philosophy-and-physics-of-duality-9780198846338"} ISBN:9780198846338
          %h3#relation_to_adscft Relation to AdS/CFT
          %p
            Relation to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/AdS%2FCFT"} AdS/CFT
            and
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/conformal+bootstrap"} conformal bootstrap
          %ul
            %li#ChesterPerlmutter18
              Shai M. Chester,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Eric+Perlmutter"} Eric Perlmutter
              %em
                M-Theory Reconstruction from
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mn 2
                      %mo ,
                      %mn 0
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (2,0)
                CFT and the Chiral Algebra Conjecture
              (
              %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1805.00892"}> arXiv:1805.00892
              )
          %h3#cohomological_considerations Cohomological considerations
          %p
            Discussion of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cohomology"} cohomological
            charge quantization in type II (
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/RR-fields"} RR-fields
            as cocycles in
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/KR-theory"} KR-theory
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/supergravity+C-field"} supergravity C-field
            is in
          %ul
            %li#FMW00
              D. Diaconescu,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Gregory+Moore"} Gregory Moore
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Edward+Witten"} Edward Witten
              = succeed "," do
                %em
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi E
                          %mn 8
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E_8
                  Gauge Theory, and a Derivation of K-Theory from M-Theory
              = succeed ")," do
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/0005090"} arXiv:hep-th/0005090
              %em A Derivation of K-Theory from M-Theory
              (
              %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/0005091"}> arXiv:hep-th/0005091
              )
          %p See also
          %ul
            %li#GarciaUranga05
              Inaki Garcia-Etxebarria,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Angel+Uranga"} Angel Uranga
              = succeed "," do
                %em From F/M-theory to K-theory and back
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/0510073"} arXiv:hep-th/0510073
          %p
            For more on this perspective as 10d type II as a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/self-dual+higher+gauge+theory"} self-dual higher gauge theory
            in the boudnary of a kind of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/higher+dimensional+Chern-Simons+theory"} 11-d Chern-Simons theory
            is in
          %ul
            %li#BelovMooreII
              Dmitriy Belov,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Greg+Moore"} Greg Moore
              %em Type II Actions from 11-Dimensional Chern-Simons Theories
              (
              %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/0611020"}> arXiv:hep-th/0611020
              )
          %p
            More complete discussion of the decomposition of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/supergravity+C-field"} supergravity C-field
            as one passes from 11d to 10d is in
          %ul
            %li#MathaiSati03
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Varghese+Mathai"}> Varghese Mathai
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hisham+Sati"} Hisham Sati
              = succeed "," do
                %em Some Relations between Twisted K-theory and E8 Gauge Theory
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/0312033"} arXiv:hep-th/0312033
          %h3#relation_to_dbrane_mechanics
            Relation to D
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mn 0
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 0
            \-brane mechanics
          %p
            Discussion of M-theory as arising from
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/type+II+string+theory"} type II string theory
            via the effect of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/D0-branes"} D0-branes
            is in
          %ul#BanksFischlerShenkerSusskind97
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Tom+Banks"}> Tom Banks
              , W. Fischler, S.H. Shenker,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Leonard+Susskind"} Leonard Susskind
              = succeed "," do
                %em M Theory As A Matrix Model: A Conjecture
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/9610043"} arXiv:hep-th/9610043
          %ul#Polchinski99
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Joseph+Polchinski"}> Joseph Polchinski
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em M-Theory and the Light Cone
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/9903165"} arXiv:hep-th/9903165
          %h3#more_on_the_relation_to_type_iia_string_theory More on the relation to type IIA string theory
          %ul
            %li#Sen97
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ashoke+Sen"}> Ashoke Sen
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em A Note on Enhanced Gauge Symmetries in M- and String Theory
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/9707123"} arXiv:hep-th/9707123
          %h3#in_terms_of_higher_geometry In terms of higher geometry
          %p
            Discussion of phenomena of M-theory in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/higher+geometry"} higher geometry
            and
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/generalized+cohomology"} generalized cohomology
            is in
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hisham+Sati"}> Hisham Sati
              ,
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Geometric+and+topological+structures+related+to+M-branes"} Geometric and topological structures related to M-branes
              (2010)
          %p
            See also the references at
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/exceptional+generalized+geometry"} exceptional generalized geometry
          %p
            In fact, much of the broad structure of M-theory and its relation to the various
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/string+theory"} string theory
            limits can be seen from the classification of exceptional
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super+L-%E2%88%9E+algebras"} super L-∞ algebras
            (such as the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/supergravity+Lie+3-algebra"} supergravity Lie 3-algebra
            and the
            = succeed ")," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/supergravity+Lie+6-algebra"} supergravity Lie 6-algebra
          %ul
            %li#FSS13
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Domenico+Fiorenza"}> Domenico Fiorenza
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hisham+Sati"} Hisham Sati
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Urs+Schreiber"} Urs Schreiber
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/schreiber/show/The+brane+bouquet"} Super Lie n-algebra extensions, higher WZW models and super p-branes with tensor multiplet fields
              (
              %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1308.5264"}> arXiv:1308.5264
              )
          %p Review:
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Branislav+Jur%C4%8Do"}> Branislav Jurčo
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Christian+Saemann"} Christian Saemann
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Urs+Schreiber"} Urs Schreiber
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Martin+Wolf"} Martin Wolf
                (eds.)
              %p
                %strong Proceedings of the LMS/EPSRC Durham Symposium on
              %p
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Higher+Structures+in+M-Theory+2018"} Higher Structures in M-Theory 2018
              %p Fortschritte der Physik Special Issue
              %p Volume 67, Issue 8-9
              %p
                %a{:href => "https://www.onlinelibrary.wiley.com/toc/15213978/2019/67/8-9"} doi:10.1002/prop.201870081
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Domenico+Fiorenza"}> Domenico Fiorenza
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hisham+Sati"} Hisham Sati
                = succeed ":" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Urs+Schreiber"} Urs Schreiber
              %p
                %strong
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/schreiber/show/The+rational+higher+structure+of+M-theory"} The Rational Higher Structure of M‐theory
              %p
                in: Proceedings of
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Higher+Structures+in+M-Theory+2018"} Higher Structures in M-Theory 2018
              %p
                Fortschritte der Physik, Special Issue
                %strong 67
                8-9
              %p
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1903.02834"}> arXiv:1903.02834
                ,
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1002/prop.201910017"} doi:10.1002/prop.201910017
          %p#ThisAnalysisReveals
            This analysis reveals, in particular, that
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/rational+homotopy+theory"} rationally
            the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/supergravity+C-field"} M-theory C-field
            (and hence
            = succeed "-charge)" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/M-brane"} M-brane
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/flux+quantization"} flux quantized
            in (unstable/
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/non-abelian+cohomology"}> non-abelian
            )
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cohomotopy+theory"} Cohomotopy theory
            in a way directly analogous to how the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/RR-field"} string theory RR-field
            is
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/charge+quantization"} flux quantized
            = succeed ";" do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/K-theory+classification+of+D-brane+charge"} in K-theory
          %ul
            %li#Sati13
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hisham+Sati"}> Hisham Sati
              ,
              %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/pdf/1310.1060.pdf#page=17"} Sec 2.5
              of:
              = succeed "," do
                %em Framed M-branes, corners, and topological invariants
              %strong 59
              (2018), 062304 (
              %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1310.1060"}> arXiv:1310.1060
              )
          %p
            The natural hypothesis that, therefore, the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/supergravity+C-field"} M-theory C-field
            should find its proper mathematical definition as a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cocycle"} cocycle
            in (not just
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/rationalization"} rationalized
            but) full-blown (
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/twisted+Cohomotopy"}> twisted
            ,
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivariant+Cohomotopy"} equivariant
            \&amp;
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differential+Cohomotopy"} differential
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/non-abelian+cohomology"} non-abelian
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cohomotopy+theory"} Cohomotopy theory
            is supported by some evidence, see at
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hypothesis+H"} Hypothesis H
            for more.
